{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00296",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.81,
      "end_seconds": 4.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Oh, morning, doctor, I hope I'm not interrupting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.36,
      "end_seconds": 12.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Yes, come in, take a seat. What can I do for you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.29,
      "end_seconds": 19.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Doctor, it's wheezing. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.67,
      "end_seconds": 22.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.11,
      "end_seconds": 31.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Uh, it's been three days, I'm fairly sure. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.59,
      "end_seconds": 35.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Is it constant, or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.47,
      "end_seconds": 38.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "It's on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.93,
      "end_seconds": 41.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Hold on, the screen's frozen for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.58,
      "end_seconds": 60.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Okay, continuing. Let me check a few things. Any runny nose or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.33,
      "end_seconds": 63.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.42,
      "end_seconds": 68.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Mm. Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.74,
      "end_seconds": 73.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Okay, so I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.44,
      "end_seconds": 82.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.59,
      "end_seconds": 86.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Um, yes, aspirin, it gives me wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.83,
      "end_seconds": 90.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.38,
      "end_seconds": 103.7,
      "duration_seconds": 12.32,
      "text": "Not at the moment, um, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.12,
      "end_seconds": 106.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.89,
      "end_seconds": 108.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "My grandmother had breast cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.89,
      "end_seconds": 124.23,
      "duration_seconds": 14.34,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.56,
      "end_seconds": 129.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.0,
      "end_seconds": 132.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.81,
      "end_seconds": 136.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "No, I've never had anything serious."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.74,
      "end_seconds": 140.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.9,
      "end_seconds": 142.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.43,
      "end_seconds": 145.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Are you on any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.31,
      "end_seconds": 147.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "No, nothing regular."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.09,
      "end_seconds": 151.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.59,
      "end_seconds": 156.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.89,
      "end_seconds": 159.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.51,
      "end_seconds": 163.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Just my gallbladder removed, in 2016."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.64,
      "end_seconds": 169.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Alright, is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.27,
      "end_seconds": 179.47,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.46,
      "end_seconds": 182.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.77,
      "end_seconds": 189.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "Yeah, busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.45,
      "end_seconds": 204.03,
      "duration_seconds": 13.58,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.37,
      "end_seconds": 206.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.75,
      "end_seconds": 222.18,
      "duration_seconds": 14.43,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression from what you've said is this: I think we're dealing with an asthma flare-up at this stage. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had wheezing for three days, and no chest pain or runny nose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.08,
      "end_seconds": 224.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.84,
      "end_seconds": 239.79,
      "duration_seconds": 14.95,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.51,
      "end_seconds": 242.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.14,
      "end_seconds": 270.23,
      "duration_seconds": 27.09,
      "text": "We should do a peak flow reading for asthma control. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'm prescribing prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day, for five days. That should help with asthma flare-up. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Let me watch you use the inhaler, a lot of people don't get the full dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.95,
      "end_seconds": 290.13,
      "duration_seconds": 16.18,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. Keep an eye out, and if the inhaler isn't helping or you can't speak in full sentences, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.33,
      "end_seconds": 296.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.29,
      "end_seconds": 306.04,
      "duration_seconds": 8.75,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in a week. Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.37,
      "end_seconds": 314.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "So, I take the prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day and come back in a week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.29,
      "end_seconds": 319.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Wonderful, I think that's it. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.66,
      "end_seconds": 324.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Right, I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.09,
      "end_seconds": 325.95,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}